{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791590765,"nonce":"+x8h3A6gkoRcQ9/e5AZApv1fuME=","title":"Notches: authoring API and addon binding","message":"A notch is a shape a rounded box cannot make, drawn in place of the element's box:\n- four signed corner radii; a negative radius is a concave corner that curves out to the element's edge, as a menu-bar dropdown meets its bar;\n- a modifier at the centre of the top edge and of the bottom edge: Scoop(width, depth, radius?), Bulge(width, height, radius?), Cut(width, depth) or Peak(width, height).\n\nConcave corners and outward modifiers lie inside the element's box, so the body is inset by them and the content needs padding. Signed radii animate through zero, from convex to concave.\n\nState (checked 2026-10-10)\n- Renderer: done. src/renderer/gpu/sdf.ts has isNotch, sdNotch and notchEdge, and src/renderer/records.ts has record rows 25 to 27 (notchCorners, notchTop, notchBottom). The shadow shader handles them too.\n- blinc_abi: done on the scene side. Scene::set_notch(node, Option\u003c[[f32; 4]; 3]\u003e) in src/scene.rs. The twelve floats are the four radii, then the top and bottom edges as (kind, width, height, radius). Kind is 0 none, 1 scoop, 2 bulge, 3 cut, 4 peak.\n- Missing: native/src has no binding for set_notch, and there is no TypeScript API for it.\n\nScope\n- A typed Notch value with the four edge kinds and helpers (a concave-top dropdown is the common one), and an encoder to the twelve floats.\n- A node or host API to set one, constant or reactive. A signal or computed is followed with an effect, and the notch is cleared when its owner is cleaned up, through the existing reactive primitives.\n- The addon binding to Scene::set_notch.\n- Pixel tests, offscreen and at 1x and 2x:\n  - a concave-top dropdown, a peak tooltip, an island scoop, a bulge and a cut;\n  - a notch with a border, with an outer shadow and with an inset shadow;\n  - a notch animating its radius through zero.\n\nOpen\n- Naming. corner-shape already has the keywords scoop and notch (host.ts cornerKeywords, and the corner-scoop and corner-notch utilities), which are per-corner superellipse shapes and a different thing. The notch value's Scoop modifier and the word notch itself overlap with them, so the property, the type and the helpers need names that do not read as the same feature.\n- Whether CSS can reach it (a declaration the cascade resolves) or only the typed API can.\n\nRelated\n- Borders are about to take layout space: blinc_abi will set Taffy's border from the painted border widths, so a border insets the content box as in CSS. Owned contexts already do this in set_border, so blinc_ts's geometry may not change. Write the notch-with-border test against that behaviour once it lands.\n- Reference design, for structure: ashui's haxe/ashui/types/Notch.hx (the value, concaveTop, encode), the bindNotch method of haxe/ashui/ui/Div.hx, and tools/snapshot/scenes/Notches.hx and NotchCompare.hx for visual references.\n\nRequested through another session working on the user's behalf. Not started.","files":null}]}